  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607184200: Verified TLS transport semantics and downgrade closure

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-18

## Context

ADR-2607184100 implemented TLS wrapping but had no live handshake evidence.
Conformance work also found that rejecting a mismatched server name while
retaining the original TCP handle would permit a guest to fall back to
plaintext after requesting TLS.

## Decision

`tls-open` is an affine transition: it consumes the TCP handle before any
validation or handshake result. A server-name mismatch closes the socket and
returns zero; the original handle cannot be reused. A successful transition
enables SNI and HTTPS endpoint identification, completes the handshake, and
returns a new opaque TLS handle.

The provider accepts an explicitly injected SSLSocketFactory for scoped test
or deployment trust policy and otherwise uses the JVM default trust roots.
The conformance test generates a one-day test-only certificate with localhost
SAN, starts a real loopback TLS server, and drives connect, TLS open, write,
read, and close through actual Wasm imports. A negative test proves a mismatched
server name yields zero, consumes the handle, closes the peer connection, and
cannot downgrade to plaintext.

## Maturity boundary

Local TLS mechanics and downgrade behavior are now executable evidence.
External PKI interoperability, revocation policy, browser/Node providers,
general component linking, production CI/soak, and Q9 cutover remain pending.
"}]
